 :base  "main"
 ;; The code owners of every file (.github/CODEOWNERS): GitHub logins with Write access. With
 ;; "Require review from Code Owners" in the main ruleset, a pull request merges only with the
 ;; approval of one of them; the agent's approval never counts. Add a colleague here.
 :owners ["u473t8"]
 ;; The agent's own GitHub account. `kit init` points Claude sessions at it through the
 ;; per-machine .claude/settings.local.json; `:agent nil` in kit.edn turns that off.
 ;; The owner logs it in once per machine, in their own terminal:
 ;;   GH_CONFIG_DIR=~/.config/gh-agent gh auth login --hostname github.com --git-protocol https --web --scopes project,workflow
 :agent {:login         "u473t8-angel"
         :email         "355360088+u473t8-angel@users.noreply.github.com"
         :gh-config-dir "~/.config/gh-agent"}}
